
0) First generate the lookup table using the resample map.py script for 
appropriate distance seperation for Tx. This can be done on waypoints that 
have been saved before which makes it easier.

1) Run the roslaunch cerpmv3 cerpm_collect if the Rx is connected and 
   you want to read in the cerpms and save them.

2) If you have already done step one, you can run the get_cerpms to save all the cerpms with their lat/lon from the lookup table.

3) Once you have cerpms saved in the csv with their lat/long, we need to run the get_path which also runs the 
get_cerpm as a subprocess so you can skip step 2. 

